questions.questionText:
In a certain code language,

A + B means &lsquo;A is the mother of B&rsquo;

A &ndash; B means &lsquo;A is the brother of B&rsquo;

A × B means &lsquo;A is the wife of B&rsquo; and

A &divide; B means &lsquo;A is the father of B&rsquo;.

How is M related to Q if &lsquo;M + N × O &divide; P &ndash; Q&rsquo;?

questions.explanation:
Given:

&lsquo;buy some food&rsquo; → &lsquo;lr tp nx&rsquo;

&lsquo;food is tasty&rsquo; → &lsquo;nx ze jq&rsquo;

Therefore, food → nx

Hence, the correct answer is **"Option 2".**

